#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed the work plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:94
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Seeds one bean per top-level content object the author named, positioned after scaffolding but before the Pages probe — a work plan exists for a folio whose publication status is not yet known, rather than waiting on that answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Somebody said \"create a folio\": work out which request they meant, with the branch computed by a decision table that may answer \"ask\", and what has to be true before anything is written. folio-assistant — getting started: from \"create a folio\" to a live site. \"Create a folio\" is five different requests. Gateway_Intent computes which one from decisions/folio-intent.dmn rather than letting the agent assume, and `ask` is one of the outcomes the table can return. Gateway_Live applies the same construction to publication, with `unknown` kept distinct from `not-yet`. Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:232
#. Diagram label
msgid "Start the Pages build and derive the URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:213
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The first beans: what the author said they want to get started on, one bean per top-level content object they named."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:196
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The misspeak case. The user has a folio and wants a document in it; this process ends and authoring-a-document.bpmn or authoring-a-paper.bpmn begins. Ending here rather than scaffolding is the whole value of the triage."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:152
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The question is presented as a short list of selectable options, never as free prose, and the list names the top-level content types the agent knows about. The answer becomes the statedIntent fact and the table is evaluated again — the user's answer is read as evidence, like any other fact."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:174
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Three questions the scan cannot answer: import these or not; library or content for each group; leave the files where they are or reorganize to declutter. Plus whether to dispatch one ingestion agent or a small swarm. Non-relaxable: nobody's files are moved or imported on inference."
msgstr ""

